        "title": "Modern Synthetic Rope: UHMWPE, Aramid, Vectran, PBO",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "High-performance synthetic fibers represent a 10–100× improvement over natural fibers and 5–15× over commodity synthetics. The performance comes from polymer chain orientation: in UHMWPE, crystalline regions of highly oriented molecular chains approach theoretical tensile efficiency. The tradeoffs are UV degradation, thermal sensitivity, or bending fatigue — a different limitation for each fiber family."
    },
